The Concept: Building a rigid multidimensional reporting matrix that dynamically reclassifies user behavior while utilizing a "Cartesian Scaffold"
            to guarantee continuous reporting dimensions (forcing zeroes where data is entirely absent).
Skills Used: Cartesian Scaffolding (UNION ALL), Dynamic Data Re-classification (CASE WHEN), Multi-stage Aggregations (COUNT(DISTINCT)), Handling Sparse Datasets.

Designed a dynamic data classification pipeline to evaluate daily multidimensional user behavior, programmatically relabeling entity categories based on concurrent interaction thresholds.
Engineered a Cartesian scaffolding matrix utilizing UNION ALL across distinct timeline variables to enforce a rigid reporting structure, successfully mitigating data sparsity issues by zero-filling absent categories.
Optimized final metric aggregations by executing COUNT(DISTINCT) and arithmetic sums across synthesized data layers, ensuring complete and gapless business intelligence reporting.
